AGNT-cursor — done 2026-08-16

Ordering followed: 3.3 -> 3.1 -> 2.3.

Task 3.3 (preservation guard) — DONE, DOOR (cursor-finish, bash, cursor path
only). cleanup() now: parks a detached HEAD onto a branch before anything
else; attempts to preserve dirty state via commit; re-checks
`git status --porcelain`; keeps the directory + branch and logs path/branch/
unpreserved-count if still dirty (pre-commit hook refusal); only removes the
worktree and deletes the branch once the tree is clean. Idempotent by
construction (verified via direct double-invocation on both outcomes).
Evidence: real fixture repo, real pre-commit hooks (permissive and
refusing), both outcomes quoted to Tower board
(agent-core/worktree-lifecycle).

Task 3.1 (arm the trap) — DONE, DOOR (cursor-finish, bash, cursor path
only). `trap cleanup EXIT` armed immediately after `resolve_git_root`, before
the SPINE/LATCH executable checks, so every die()/crash/normal-exit from that
point on reaps via the same idempotent cleanup(). Bash preserves the
original `exit N` status through an EXIT trap unless the trap itself calls
exit (verified with a standalone repro); no wrapper needed. End-to-end:
forced a real die (missing cursor-spine) with two pre-existing dirty
detached-HEAD worktrees — both preserved+removed via the trap,
`git worktree list` clean after, rc=1 preserved. Repeated with a refusing
pre-commit hook — both kept with reports, rc=1 preserved.

Task 2.3 (sparse checkout on the cursor path) — DONE, DOOR (cursor-spine,
bash, cursor path only), opt-in. cursor-agent's own `--worktree` has no
sparse flag, but it does read an untracked `.cursor/worktrees.json`
(`setup-worktree` / `setup-worktree-unix`, reverse-engineered from the
bundled index.js) synchronously before the agent starts. Proved that lever
works standalone, but it's racy for cursor-spine's actual use (shared config
file, cursor-agent reads it asynchronously in its own background process —
two concurrent spawns against the same $DIR with different partitions could
cross-read). Chose a race-free alternative: new repeatable
`cursor-spine ... --partition <path>` flag. When set, cursor-spine itself
(not cursor-agent) synchronously creates the worktree
(`git worktree add --no-checkout` + `sparse-checkout init --cone` +
`sparse-checkout set` + `checkout`) at the same path convention
cursor-finish's `worktree_path()` already expects, then passes cursor-agent
`--workspace <precreated-path>` instead of `--worktree <name>` — no shared
file, no timing dependency. Verified end-to-end through the real CLI
(`cursor-spine researcher --dir <fixture> --worktree --partition apps/api
--headless`): resulting worktree contained only root.txt + apps/api/main.py.
Default behavior (no --partition) is unchanged: full checkout via
cursor-agent's own --worktree, now with an explicit log line naming the
cost, per the "never silently narrow" law.

